#N canvas 0 0 760 970 10;
#X text 12 8 vgm-player - a VGM/VGZ file through one ym2612~ + one sn76489~ (each channel scoped);
#X text 12 28 vgm~ paces the log at its 44100 Hz timebase: outlet 0 emits `ch<k> reg <a> <d>` for the;
#X text 12 44 ONE ym2612~ (its Nuked core is the whole chip \, all six channels) \, outlet 1 carries the;
#X text 12 60 PSG chip's raw bytes into sn76489~ (3 square waves + 1 noise) \, outlet 2 is the YM2612;
#X text 12 76 DAC PCM stream \, outlet 3 bangs at the end of non-looping data.;
#X text 12 96 both chips expose per-channel signal outlets: ym2612~ outlets 1-6 = channels 1-6 \,;
#X text 12 112 sn76489~ outlets 1-4 = tone 1-3 / noise - each feeds one graph~ below (outlet 0 of;
#X text 12 128 each chip = the sum). The chip mix is NOT clipped internally - dense logs peak;
#X text 12 144 ~4x over +-1 \, so the final gain must fit that headroom (this patch: 0.2).;
#X text 12 164 demo.vgm ships with the examples - an arpeggio on channel 1. Put your own .vgm/.vgz next;
#X text 12 180 to a patch or anywhere on the pd search path.;
#X msg 40 204 load demo.vgm;
#X msg 40 232 play;
#X msg 100 232 pause;
#X msg 160 232 stop;
#X msg 220 232 goto loop;
#X msg 40 260 loop 1;
#X msg 110 260 info;
#X msg 300 204 load mad_bossa.vgm;
#X msg 300 232 load overworld.vgm;
#X msg 300 260 load sad_polka.vgm;
#X text 12 288 CC0 music (Safety Stoat Studios "Free VGMs" \, github jerellsworth/free_vgms) -;
#X text 12 304 real multi-channel songs: 3 FM voices + PSG bass/percussion each;
#X obj 40 332 vgm~;
#X obj 40 372 ym2612~;
#X obj 160 372 sn76489~;
#X obj 40 412 *~ 0.2;
#X text 110 412 gain fits the real chip-mix peak (~4.3 on the CC0 logs) - lower it further if dac~ still clips;
#X obj 40 452 dac~;
#X obj 40 492 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 492 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 480 492 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 40 602 graph~ 200 90;
#X obj 260 602 graph~ 200 90;
